# The users, sessions' records, files' records and the generated auth secret
# live in the DATABASE D1 database, the sessions in the KV namespace and the
# uploaded files in the R2_BUCKET bucket, all bound in wrangler.jsonc (the
# committed fixture render — wrangler provides local stand-ins behind each;
# `pnpm db:migrate:local` creates the tables and the secret — and, on deploy,
# rendered from the cloudflare-d1, cloudflare-kv and cloudflare-r2 roots'
# wiring documents).
#
# Nothing is required: anonymous and email-and-password sign-in work as they
# are. For GitHub or Google sign-in put a provider's client id AND secret in
# apps/web/.dev.vars (wrangler dev) or .env.local (next dev) — never commit
# them. The OAuth app's callback URL is <origin>/api/auth/callback/<provider>.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
